@page "/datagrid-ai-highlight"

<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.H2" TagName="TagName.H1" class="rz-pt-8">
    Blazor DataGrid <strong>AI Highlight</strong>
</RadzenText>
<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Subtitle1" TagName="TagName.P" class="rz-pb-4">
    Describe a condition in plain words and let the AI model pick the rows of a Blazor DataGrid that match it. The rows are highlighted in place while the grid keeps its paging, sorting and filtering.
</RadzenText>

<RadzenExample ComponentName="DataGrid" Example="DataGridAIHighlight">
    <DataGridAIHighlight />
</RadzenExample>

<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" class="rz-mt-8">
    The page sends a compact line per order and the condition to the <code>IChatClient</code> from <code>IAIChatService.GetChatClient()</code>, asking for a JSON object with the matching ids and a short explanation.
    The ids go into a set that the <code>CellRender</code> handler checks to add a background to the cells of the matching rows. Unlike a filter, the user still sees the other rows and the context around the matches;
    the same idea works with <code>RowRender</code>, or for the appointments of a Scheduler or the items of a Tree.
</RadzenText>
